# main.py

`main.py` only wires the application. It does not implement behavior. Who may call whom is in `architecture-constitution.mdc`.

## Allowed here

- Create the FastAPI app and attach the lifespan
- Call bootstrap to register exception handlers, mount the `approvals`, `slack`, and `message_exchanges` routers, serve `static/index.html` at `GET /`, and mount that directory at `/static`
- On lifespan startup, create tables and start the minute scan. On shutdown, stop the scan
- Inside `if __name__ == "__main__"`, start Uvicorn with one worker

## Not allowed here

Route handlers, status transitions, SQL, Slack HTTP, callback retries, and hand-built error JSON. Those belong in the slice that owns them.

`main.py` stays within 80 lines. Bootstrap mounts the routers. `main.py` does not call `include_router` once per router. A package `__init__.py` does not re-export `router`.

The process runs one worker. Bootstrap does not start a second scan or a second callback runner.
